WEBVTT

00:01:44.651 --> 00:01:47.552
My shift'll be over in just two hours.

00:01:57.831 --> 00:02:01.768
Mihoshi! Mihoshi, please wake up!

00:02:01.768 --> 00:02:04.905
Huh? Wh-What is it, Kiyone?

00:02:04.905 --> 00:02:07.174
Yagami's engine power is failing.

00:02:07.174 --> 00:02:09.009
But we just fixed it.

00:02:09.009 --> 00:02:10.738
I don't get it.

00:02:12.379 --> 00:02:15.371
You! I told you we shouldn't take a shortcut!

00:02:16.316 --> 00:02:19.479
Wait a minute. You know
you agreed to it, Kiyone.

00:02:21.321 --> 00:02:24.658
Mihoshi, I think this might
be what they call Sargasso.

00:02:24.658 --> 00:02:26.693
What? What's that?

00:02:26.693 --> 00:02:28.829
You know, the spaceship graveyard.

00:02:28.829 --> 00:02:32.321
They say you never get out
once you wander into this area.

00:02:37.237 --> 00:02:40.900
Uh-oh, Kiyone.
What do you think that is, huh?

00:03:00.594 --> 00:03:01.928
What?

00:03:01.928 --> 00:03:04.624
Hey, now. What's going on here, huh?

00:04:34.421 --> 00:04:36.056
Hey. Wake up.

00:04:36.056 --> 00:04:37.751
Please wake up.

00:04:48.501 --> 00:04:50.937
- Who are you?
- My name's Mirei.

00:04:50.937 --> 00:04:53.405
How about you and me have fun?

00:05:03.016 --> 00:05:04.847
Where did you come from?

00:05:11.458 --> 00:05:13.326
From that ship over there.

00:05:13.326 --> 00:05:15.191
Wow!

00:05:18.398 --> 00:05:20.389
What is it?

00:05:20.967 --> 00:05:22.802
Stop that!

00:05:22.802 --> 00:05:24.537
Her name is Ryo-Ohki.

00:05:24.537 --> 00:05:27.131
Don't worry. She's not gonna bite you.

00:05:31.311 --> 00:05:33.413
She's afraid of me.

00:05:33.413 --> 00:05:35.711
Knock it off! I'm ticklish, you know!

00:05:48.628 --> 00:05:50.730
By the way, my name is Sasami.

00:05:50.730 --> 00:05:53.700
Say, how did you get in here anyway, Mirei?

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:55.565
Do you want me to show you?

00:05:57.070 --> 00:05:58.662
Yeah!

00:06:01.207 --> 00:06:03.402
Hold on tight, okay?

00:06:19.059 --> 00:06:20.788
Sasami!

00:06:31.738 --> 00:06:34.074
Ayeka! Ryoko!

00:06:34.074 --> 00:06:36.676
What's wrong? What are
you doing up this late?

00:06:36.676 --> 00:06:38.611
What's the matter, Tenchi?

00:06:38.611 --> 00:06:42.282
Sasami and Ryo-Ohki have
disappeared into the bedroom mirror!

00:06:42.282 --> 00:06:43.909
What?!

00:06:44.884 --> 00:06:47.520
Tenchi, there's something in the bathroom.

00:06:47.520 --> 00:06:49.010
No!

00:07:05.605 --> 00:07:07.835
This is such a gorgeous room!

00:07:12.846 --> 00:07:14.047
Please, help yourself.

00:07:14.047 --> 00:07:17.350
Incredible! It's like magic, huh?

00:07:17.350 --> 00:07:19.409
I'll take some of these.

00:07:24.357 --> 00:07:27.694
Hey, Sasami, why aren't you afraid of me?

00:07:27.694 --> 00:07:29.184
Why should I be?

00:07:30.196 --> 00:07:33.063
Because I'm... you know...

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:37.837
Oh, about that. Ryoko can go
through walls and stuff too, you know.

00:07:37.837 --> 00:07:39.939
You mean, like me?

00:07:39.939 --> 00:07:43.009
Is that because you
have ESP or something?

00:07:43.009 --> 00:07:44.577
I don't know.

00:07:44.577 --> 00:07:48.570
I've always been alone, so
I don't really know how I do it.

00:07:50.583 --> 00:07:53.643
The only clue I have left is that photograph.

00:08:03.196 --> 00:08:05.632
The dress you're wearing, it's so pretty.

00:08:05.632 --> 00:08:09.033
Well, how would you
like to try one on, Sasami?

00:08:31.024 --> 00:08:32.514
There.

00:08:36.629 --> 00:08:38.859
Are you all right, Sasami?

00:08:40.166 --> 00:08:44.296
- Come on, let's go.
I'll give you a tour of the ship.
- Yeah.

00:09:03.256 --> 00:09:07.026
So, Washu, what do you think?
Can you figure any of this out?

00:09:07.026 --> 00:09:08.895
Well, considering the size of that ship,

00:09:08.895 --> 00:09:13.066
it should have just about
the same power as Yagami does.

00:09:13.066 --> 00:09:15.401
But I can't see any trace of it.

00:09:15.401 --> 00:09:18.037
Yeah, and what does that mean?

00:09:18.037 --> 00:09:21.107
No energy. The ship
doesn't have any output.

00:09:21.107 --> 00:09:24.440
In other words, that ship is dead.

00:09:52.839 --> 00:09:55.074
Are you ready, everyone? Here we go.

00:09:55.074 --> 00:09:56.564
Mm-hmm.

00:10:14.594 --> 00:10:17.063
That noise... I'm scared.

00:10:17.063 --> 00:10:19.198
I don't hear anything.

00:10:19.198 --> 00:10:21.567
Let's go back, please.

00:10:21.567 --> 00:10:23.436
We just got here, Mihoshi.

00:10:23.436 --> 00:10:27.372
This must be a ghost ship.
What else could it be?

00:10:28.241 --> 00:10:30.436
Calm down. You're imagining things.

00:10:33.913 --> 00:10:36.279
Wait for me!

00:10:43.189 --> 00:10:46.826
The level of ions in the air
is increasing considerably.

00:10:46.826 --> 00:10:49.796
This is exciting to
gather such valuable data.

00:10:49.796 --> 00:10:54.467
I wonder if it's because the materialized
ectoplasm is ethereal in nature.

00:10:54.467 --> 00:10:58.836
Washu, we're looking for Sasami.
First things first, okay, please?

00:11:19.125 --> 00:11:20.693
Hey, that's my sister!

00:11:20.693 --> 00:11:22.295
Oh? Which one?

00:11:22.295 --> 00:11:25.321
That one with the long hair.

00:11:26.165 --> 00:11:28.534
I can't see. Can you find
a switch anywhere, Ryoko?

00:11:28.534 --> 00:11:30.331
It's really so dark in here,
and we need some light.

00:11:39.879 --> 00:11:42.109
Hey, what is it, Ayeka?

00:11:47.920 --> 00:11:50.150
Sa-Sasami!

00:11:57.830 --> 00:12:00.133
It seems like a regular mirror to me.

00:12:00.133 --> 00:12:03.436
But I just saw Sasami's reflection in there.

00:12:03.436 --> 00:12:06.072
Ayeka, I really think you're seeing things.

00:12:06.072 --> 00:12:07.937
Sasa...!

00:12:09.008 --> 00:12:11.377
Sasami? Sasami?

00:12:11.377 --> 00:12:15.473
Stop banging your head like that.
Your face is going to warp.

00:12:17.750 --> 00:12:20.253
Yeah!

00:12:20.253 --> 00:12:22.355
Oh, that was so close.

00:12:22.355 --> 00:12:24.721
But it sure was fun, wasn't it?

00:12:27.827 --> 00:12:32.365
Mirei, hey, let's trick them a little bit more.

00:12:32.365 --> 00:12:34.731
What do you mean, trick them?

00:12:52.819 --> 00:12:54.854
Here they come.

00:12:54.854 --> 00:12:56.055
What's this place?

00:12:56.055 --> 00:12:58.148
It looks like a ballroom, doesn't it?

00:13:09.368 --> 00:13:11.131
It's just a mirror.

00:13:32.191 --> 00:13:34.022
Sasami!

00:13:37.697 --> 00:13:39.562
Sasami!

00:13:45.271 --> 00:13:46.539
Washu, look!

00:13:46.539 --> 00:13:49.975
What? Whoa!

00:13:59.852 --> 00:14:04.257
Wow! That must be an ethereal life-form.

00:14:04.257 --> 00:14:07.360
I wonder if it's even
possible to collect a sample.

00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:11.030
Washu, forget about that.
We have to find Sasami.

00:14:11.030 --> 00:14:13.599
Why didn't you grab that thing for me?

00:14:13.599 --> 00:14:15.157
Oh, man.

00:14:17.837 --> 00:14:21.641
Wow, that was a lot of fun.

00:14:21.641 --> 00:14:25.511
Hey, wait, Sasami. Can you
close your eyes for a second?

00:14:25.511 --> 00:14:26.978
Yeah.

00:14:53.839 --> 00:14:55.898
It's my garden at home.

00:14:57.043 --> 00:14:59.978
I can see it in your mind, Sasami.

00:15:20.566 --> 00:15:23.364
Let's go this way. We have a maze.

00:15:35.014 --> 00:15:38.040
This was one of my favorite places.

00:15:48.694 --> 00:15:49.929
Look.

00:15:49.929 --> 00:15:52.557
There's the ribbon I tied as a signpost.

00:15:54.467 --> 00:15:57.368
There's a fountain at the end of this maze.

00:16:03.175 --> 00:16:05.878
You shouldn't cheat like that.

00:16:05.878 --> 00:16:08.574
Don't you want to get there quickly, Sasami?

00:16:17.590 --> 00:16:19.759
This is kind of strange, isn't it?

00:16:19.759 --> 00:16:20.893
Yeah.

00:16:20.893 --> 00:16:23.696
I used to cut study hall
and come over here a lot

00:16:23.696 --> 00:16:25.665
and they were always so mad at me.

00:16:25.665 --> 00:16:27.800
I envy you, Sasami.

00:16:27.800 --> 00:16:29.802
So you really are a princess, huh?

00:16:29.802 --> 00:16:34.466
It's not a good thing to be a princess.
You have to be so polite and proper.

00:16:42.014 --> 00:16:44.417
- Catch!
- Aah! That's cold!

00:16:44.417 --> 00:16:46.044
Sneak attack!

00:16:51.824 --> 00:16:53.993
I'm soaking wet! It's great!

00:16:53.993 --> 00:16:55.795
Yeah, me, too.

00:16:55.795 --> 00:16:59.663
Hey, let's take a roller
coaster ride. That should dry us.

00:17:09.375 --> 00:17:11.775
Now we go over the super loop! All right!

00:17:20.953 --> 00:17:22.788
I've been on this on Earth.

00:17:22.788 --> 00:17:25.124
I love merry-go-rounds.

00:17:25.124 --> 00:17:29.729
In your mind the memory of this ride
had a sticker saying, "Two thumbs up."

00:17:29.729 --> 00:17:32.061
And it had sparkling hearts all over it.

00:17:35.701 --> 00:17:38.898
It's things that are beautiful and dear to me.

00:17:39.939 --> 00:17:41.974
You're absolutely right, Mirei.

00:17:41.974 --> 00:17:44.465
Only my favorite memories
get one of those stickers.

00:17:47.947 --> 00:17:50.616
Wow. Now, this is how I remember fireworks.

00:17:50.616 --> 00:17:55.110
- Does this have a sticker too?
- Yep. It's got an ultra-super jumbo sticker.

00:18:01.894 --> 00:18:04.764
I think I should go.

00:18:04.764 --> 00:18:06.665
But why?

00:18:06.665 --> 00:18:09.463
'Cause everybody will
be so worried about me.

00:18:10.202 --> 00:18:11.829
What?

00:18:15.040 --> 00:18:17.008
They disappeared.

00:18:19.712 --> 00:18:22.415
The thing is...

00:18:22.415 --> 00:18:26.408
...it is impossible for the mind
to be in two places at once.

00:18:34.260 --> 00:18:36.728
Mirei, I'm sorry.

00:18:37.663 --> 00:18:38.998
That's all right.

00:18:38.998 --> 00:18:41.364
I had a lot of fun, Sasami.

00:18:42.535 --> 00:18:45.004
Mirei, promise we'll meet again.

00:18:45.004 --> 00:18:48.274
- Mm-hmm.
- I'll be back. Let's look forward to that.

00:18:48.274 --> 00:18:50.309
Mm-hmm, all right.

00:18:50.309 --> 00:18:55.679
It's awful, but I don't have anything
to offer you as a token of our friendship.

00:19:01.253 --> 00:19:05.121
You've already given me something:
Your warm feelings, Sasami.

00:19:11.430 --> 00:19:13.227
Bye-bye, Ryo-Ohki.

00:19:15.367 --> 00:19:17.232
Let's go now.

00:19:20.406 --> 00:19:22.808
Oh, failure.

00:19:22.808 --> 00:19:26.445
Next time, we have to go better prepared.

00:19:26.445 --> 00:19:28.436
Sasami.

00:19:36.522 --> 00:19:38.012
Mirei?

00:19:44.730 --> 00:19:46.721
I guess she's gone.

00:19:52.905 --> 00:19:55.808
Hi! I'm back!

00:19:55.808 --> 00:19:57.142
Sasami.

00:19:57.142 --> 00:19:59.245
Sasami!

00:19:59.245 --> 00:20:02.882
Sasami, where have you been?

00:20:02.882 --> 00:20:05.442
Sec... ret.

00:20:18.330 --> 00:20:19.532
What's happening?

00:20:19.532 --> 00:20:23.434
Well, I think the power is
back on and Yagami can fly.

00:20:33.646 --> 00:20:36.308
Bye-bye, Mirei.

00:22:52.451 --> 00:22:57.289
Our spaceship Yagami is hijacked
while we're eating at a drive-in restaurant.

00:22:57.289 --> 00:23:00.325
Oh, no! Come back, my Yagami!

00:23:00.325 --> 00:23:02.561
Hey, you! Hold it!

00:23:02.561 --> 00:23:05.030
The culprits are a couple
of young space gangsters.

00:23:05.030 --> 00:23:08.834
We zoom after Yagami at breakneck speed.

00:23:08.834 --> 00:23:12.805
And ahead of us,
a supernova is blocking our way!

00:23:12.805 --> 00:23:14.973
Coming up next is "No Need for Runaways!"

00:23:14.973 --> 00:23:17.810
The terrifying countdown
rips through space!

00:23:17.810 --> 00:23:20.438
It's unquestionably busy!
